# Kimi + Claude family model — dispatch architecture (v1.27.0)

Alias namespace contract. `claudeN`/`kimiN` are native accounts; `<id>` (no
prefix) is always Claude Code; `kimi-<id>` is always Kimi Code on the same
backend; `kc-<id>` is Claude Code on a Kimi-native backend (legacy renamed).

flowchart TB
  subgraph NativeAccounts["Native accounts (isolated homes)"]
    C1["claudeN → CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-&lt;n&gt;<br/>cma_run → claude (Claude Code)"]
    K1["kimiN  → KIMI_CODE_HOME=~/.kimi-code-&lt;n&gt;<br/>cma_run_kimi → kimi (Kimi Code CLI)"]
  end

  subgraph ProviderEngine["Provider engine (shared)"]
    SYNC["claude-providers sync<br/>verify · status.json · emit aliases"]
    KA["~/.claude-prov-&lt;id&gt;<br/>(Claude Code home)"]
    KP["~/.kimi-prov-&lt;id&gt;/config.toml<br/>(Kimi Code home)"]
  end

  subgraph Backends["Backends"]
    P["&lt;id&gt; provider (deepseek, …)<br/>same backend, same key"]
    KIMINATIVE["Kimi native backend (kc-*)"]
  end

  subgraph Aliases["Alias namespace"]
    A1["&lt;id&gt;  = cma_run_provider &lt;id&gt;"]
    A2["kimi-&lt;id&gt; = cma_run_kimi_provider &lt;id&gt;"]
    A3["kc-&lt;id&gt; = cma_run_provider kc-&lt;id&gt;"]
  end

  C1 -->|"claudeN (native)"| CLAUDE_AGENT["Claude Code agent"]
  K1 -->|"kimiN (native)"| KIMI_AGENT["Kimi Code agent"]

  SYNC --> A1
  SYNC --> A2
  A1 -->|"Claude Code"| CLAUDE_AGENT
  A1 --> CLAUDE_AGENT --> P
  A2 --> KIMI_AGENT --> P
  A2 -. "shared status.json gate" .-> KA
  SYNC --> KP
  A3 -->|"Claude Code over Kimi native (legacy)"| CLAUDE_AGENT

  CLAUDE_AGENT --> KA
  KIMI_AGENT --> KP
  KA --> P
  KP --> P
  CLAUDE_AGENT --> KIMINATIVE
